---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Doc from '../components/Doc.astro';
import { APP_STORE_NAME } from '../consts';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Amplifly's privacy policy. Everything you log is stored on your device and synced to your account; every algorithm runs on your device. No analytics, no advertising, no data sales."
>
  <PageHead eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lead="What Amplifly stores, where it lives, and what we never do with it. No analytics, no advertising, no data sales.">
    <p class="small">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    <p class="small">Questions? <a class="link" href="mailto:hello@amplifly.me">hello@amplifly.me</a></p>
  </PageHead>

  <Doc>

      <section id="the-short-version">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Everything you do in Amplifly — brain check-ins, flow and focus sessions, your ND profile,
          your own tools and insights, the recommendation model — is stored on your device, and every
          algorithm runs on your device. Amplifly requires an account to use, so that data also syncs
          to your account: encrypted in transit, stored encrypted at rest on Supabase's servers, and
          never sold, shared, or used for any purpose other than keeping your data available to you.
          We collect no analytics, crash reports, or advertising data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="what-data-amplifly-stores">
        <h2>What data Amplifly stores</h2>
        <p>
          The following is stored <strong>on your device</strong> using AsyncStorage, and synced to
          your account while you are signed in:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Brain check-ins (brain state + optional note + timestamp) — several per day if you update your state</li>
          <li>Flow and focus sessions (activity, duration, intensity, interest level, helpers, drains, condition used, optional note)</li>
          <li>Your ND profile (which profiles you selected, executive function rating, working memory rating)</li>
          <li>Tools you add yourself and self-insights you record</li>
          <li>Your name (optional, used only for personalized greetings)</li>
          <li>The recommendation engine's learned state (Beta posteriors per condition/context cell) and its outcome history</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Your theme and notification preferences are also stored on your device, but they are not
          synced. Reminders and Focus-timer break alerts are local notifications scheduled by your
          phone; the app does not register for push notifications.
        </p>
        <p>
          Local storage is capped so it stays bounded — the most recent 2,000 brain check-ins,
          365 flow sessions, 500 recommendation outcomes, 50 self-insights, and 100 custom tools.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="your-account">
        <h2>Your account</h2>
        <p>
          Amplifly requires an account. There is no guest or signed-out mode — when you open the app
          without an active session, you are taken to the sign-in screen. Signing up takes an email
          address and a password.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your email address is stored by Supabase for authentication. Password resets are handled by emailing you a one-time code.</li>
          <li>Your brain checks, sessions, profile, custom tools, insights, and recommender state are synced to Supabase's servers and stored encrypted at rest.</li>
          <li>Sync runs in the background and never blocks the app. Once you are signed in, Amplifly works offline — an account is required, but a live connection is not.</li>
          <li>Signing out immediately stops syncing. Your local data stays on your device. Signing in again with the same account keeps it; signing in with a different account clears the local data first.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Supabase is an open-source database platform. Their infrastructure is hosted on AWS.
          You can read Supabase's privacy and security documentation at{' '}
          <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy">supabase.com/privacy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="what-we-do-not-collect">
        <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No analytics (no Mixpanel, Amplitude, or similar)</li>
          <li>No crash reporting (no Sentry, Bugsnag, or similar)</li>
          <li>No advertising identifiers (no IDFA, GAID)</li>
          <li>No usage telemetry of any kind</li>
          <li>No data is ever sold, shared with advertisers, or used for any purpose other than the functionality described above</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="the-recommendation-engine-and-flow-forecast">
        <h2>The recommendation engine and flow forecast</h2>
        <p>
          The recommendation engine is a Thompson-sampling contextual bandit. All computation
          runs on your device. The model's learned posteriors sync to your account so your
          learning carries across devices — but nothing is used for advertising or shared with
          anyone.
        </p>
        <p>
          The flow forecast uses a small neural network trained on synthetic data built from
          published research on focus and neurodivergence. The weights are fixed and ship with
          the app — they never change on your device. The forecast is then calibrated against the
          flow sessions you have logged; that calibration is computed on the spot, not stored.
        </p>
        <p>
          {APP_STORE_NAME}, the version of Amplifly on the App Store today, uses no sensors,
          wearables, or biometric data. Everything it reasons about comes from what you tell it
          and what the phone already knows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="the-bioproxal-wearable-in-development">
        <h2>The BioProxal wearable (in development)</h2>
        <p>
          An optional BioProxal wearable integration is being built and is <strong>not part of the App
          Store release</strong>. As currently built, the wearable computes its readings on the device
          itself and sends only finished values — a flow score, heart rate, HRV, SpO2, and
          breathing rate — to the app over Bluetooth while the app is open. The app never receives
          raw sensor signals.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy describes the App Store release only. Before a wearable-enabled version is
          released, it will be updated to describe what the app stores, syncs, and does with the
          wearable's numbers, and the date at the top of this page will change.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="deleting-your-data">
        <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>
          To delete your account and all data stored in Supabase, email us at{' '}
          <a href="mailto:hello@amplifly.me?subject=Delete my account">
            hello@amplifly.me
          </a>{' '}
          with the subject "Delete my account." We will remove all rows associated with your
          user ID and delete your Supabase auth account within 7 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          To delete data stored locally on your device, uninstall the app. All AsyncStorage
          data is removed automatically when the app is uninstalled. Uninstalling does not
          delete your account or the data synced to it — email us to do that.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children">
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Amplifly is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal
          information from children under 13.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes-to-this-policy">
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the date at the top of
          this page.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy? Email{' '}
          <a href="mailto:hello@amplifly.me">hello@amplifly.me</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

  </Doc>


  <Footer />
</Layout>
